      "question": [
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381703",
          "text": "<p>The function $f(x)=\\cos x-x$</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>is an even function</li><li>is an odd function</li><li>is neither an even nor an odd function</li><li>None of these</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,functions,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381709",
          "text": "<p>Evaluate the limit<br>$$<br>\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1-\\cos x}{\\sin ^{2} x}<br>$$</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$1$</li><li>$\\frac{1}{2}$</li><li>$2$</li><li>$0$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,limits,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381694",
          "text": "<p>Evaluate $y^{\\prime \\prime}(1)$ where $y=e^{x}+x^{e}$.</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$0$</li><li>$1$</li><li>$e^{2}$</li><li>$e$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381696",
          "text": "<p>Choose the CORRECT statement -</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>The function $f(x)=\\exp \\left(-x^{2}\\right)-1$ has the root $x=0$.</li><li>If a function $f$ is differentiable on $[-1,1]$, then there is a point $x$ in that interval where $f^{\\prime}(x)=0$.</li><li>If $1$ is a root of $f$, then $f^{\\prime}(x)$ changes sign at $1 .$</li><li>If $f^{\\prime \\prime}(0)&lt;0$ and $f^{\\prime \\prime}(1)&gt;0$ then there is a point in $(0,1)$, where $f$ has an inflection point.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,multiple-selects,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381690",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following is/are FALSE?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>The absolute maximum value of $f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ on the interval $[2,4]$ is $2.$</li><li>If $f(x)$ is a continuous function and $f(3)=2$ and $f(5)=-1$, then $f(x)$ has a root between $3$ and $5 .$</li><li>The function $g(x)=2 x^{3}-12 x+5$ has $5$ real roots.</li><li>If $h(x)$ is a continuous function and $h(1)=4$ and $h(2)=5$, then $h(x)$ has no roots between $1$ and $2.$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;c;d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,maxima-minima,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381705",
          "text": "<p>The function $f(x)=x^{4}-6 x^{2}$ is increasing on the intervals</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$(0, \\sqrt{3})$ only</li><li>$(\\sqrt{3}, \\infty)$ only</li><li>$(-\\infty,-\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0, \\sqrt{3})$ only</li><li>$(-\\sqrt{3}, 0)$ and $(\\sqrt{3}, \\infty)$ only</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,maxima-minima,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381701",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following functions satisfy the conditions of Rolle's Theorem on the interval $[-1,1]?$&nbsp;<br>$$<br>\\begin{aligned}<br>&amp;f(x)=1-x^{2 / 3}\\\\<br>&amp;g(x)=x^{3}-2 x^{2}-x+2\\\\<br>&amp;h(x)=\\cos \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}(x+1)\\right)<br>\\end{aligned}<br>$$<br>Rolle's Theorem applies to:</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>both $f$ and $g$</li><li>both $g$ and $h$</li><li>$g$ only</li><li>$h$ only</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,maxima-minima,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381688",
          "text": "<p>Suppose $g(x)$ is a polynomial function such that $g(-1)=4$ and $g(2)=7$. Then there is a number $c$ between $-1$ and $2$ such that</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$g(c)=1$</li><li>$g^{\\prime}(c)=1$</li><li>$g(c)=0$</li><li>$g^{\\prime}(c)=0$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,maxima-minima,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381676",
          "text": "<p>The equation $x^{5}+x+1=0$ has a solution in the interval</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$[0,1]$</li><li>$[-1,0]$</li><li>$[-2,-1]$</li><li>$[1,2]$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,maxima-minima,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381693",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following statements:</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-roman\"><li>$f(x)$ is continuous on $[a, b]$</li><li>$f(x)$ is differentiable on $(a, b)$</li><li>$f(a)=f(b)$</li></ol><p>Which of the above statements are required in order to guarantee a $c \\in(a, b)$ such that $f^{\\prime}(c)(b-a)=f(b)-f(a) ?$</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>I only</li><li>I and II only</li><li>I, II, and III</li><li>I and III only</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,continuity-and-differentiability,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381699",
          "text": "<p>Suppose that the derivative of a function $h$ is given by:<br>$$<br>h^{\\prime}(x)=x(x-1)^{2}(x-2)<br>$$<br>On what interval(s) is $h$ increasing?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$(-\\infty, 0)$</li><li>$(-\\infty, 0)$ and $(2, \\infty)$</li><li>$(0,2)$</li><li>$(0,1)$ and $(2, \\infty)$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381684",
          "text": "<p>Suppose $f$ is twice differentiable with<br>$$<br>f^{\\prime \\prime}(x)=7 x-2, \\quad f^{\\prime}(-2)=0, \\quad \\text { and } \\quad f(-2)=-2 .<br>$$<br>Find $f(0)$.</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$-337 / 6$</li><li>$-74 / 3$</li><li>$23 / 9$</li><li>$37 / 4$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381680",
          "text": "<p>If $f(x)=e^{x} g(x), g(0)=2$ and $g^{\\prime}(0)=1$, then $f^{\\prime}(0)$ is</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$1$</li><li>$3$</li><li>$2$</li><li>$0$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,maxima-minima,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381698",
          "text": "<p>Let $q(x)$ be a continuous function which is defined for all real numbers. A portion of the graph of $q^{\\prime}(x)$, the derivative of $q(x)$, is shown below.</p><p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p><br>On which of the following interval(s) is $q(x)$ increasing?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$(0,2)$</li><li>$(2,4)$</li><li>$(7,9)$</li><li>None of these</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "b;c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,multiple-selects,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381692",
          "text": "<p>Let $I=(a, b)$ be an open interval and let $f$ be a function which is differentiable on $I$. Which of the followings is/are true statements -</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>If $f^{\\prime}(x)=0$ for all $x \\in I$, then there is a constant $r$ such that $f(x)=r$ for all $x \\in I$.</li><li>If $f^{\\prime}(x)&gt;0$ for all $x \\in I$, then $f(x)$ is strictly increasing on $I$.</li><li>If $f^{\\prime}(x)&lt;0$ for all $x \\in I$, then $f(x)$ is strictly decreasing on $I$.</li><li>If $f^{\\prime}(x)&gt;0$ for all $x \\in I$, then $f(x)$ is strictly decreasing on $I$.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,maxima-minima,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381674",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following expression evaluates to given integral<br>$$<br>\\int \\frac{\\ln (\\ln x)}{x \\ln x} d x<br>$$</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$\\dfrac{\\ln x}{x}+C$</li><li>$\\frac{1}{2}(\\ln \\ln x)^{2}+C$</li><li>$(\\ln x)^{2}+C$</li><li>$(\\ln \\ln x)+C$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,integration,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381707",
          "text": "<p>Determine the value of following limit<br>$$<br>\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty}\\left(\\sqrt{x^{2}+4 x+1}-x\\right)<br>$$</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$2$</li><li>$4$</li><li>$\\frac{1}{2}$</li><li>$3$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,limits,one-mark",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381682",
          "text": "<p>The sum of three positive numbers is $12$ and two of them are equal. Find the largest possible product.</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$86$</li><li>$64$</li><li>$48$</li><li>$72$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,maxima-minima,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381678",
          "text": "<p>Let $f$ be differentiable for all $x$. If $f(1)=-2$ and $f^{\\prime}(x) \\geq 2$ for $x \\in[1,6]$, then</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$f(6) \\geq 8$</li><li>$f(6)&lt;8$</li><li>$f(6)&lt;5$</li><li>$f(6)=5$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,differentiation,maxima-minima,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "381686",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following limit is/are correct?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$\\displaystyle{}\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} \\sqrt[x]{x}=1$</li><li>$\\displaystyle{}\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty} \\sqrt[x]{x}=e$</li><li>$\\displaystyle{}\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty}\\left(1+\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^{x}=e^{2}$</li><li>$\\displaystyle{}\\lim _{x \\rightarrow \\infty}\\left(1+\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^{x}=e$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses_2026_cs_cal_tw_1,goclasses-testseries-2026,goclasses,calculus,limits,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Calculus"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}